From 0a0127b420337a74c33a3219757a45b6660b0b76 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 15 May 2026 00:09:33 +0000
Subject: pulley: add xband_s8 + br_if fused dispatch ops
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds four new Pulley bytecode ops via for_each_op:

  xband32_s8_br_if_x32       low32(dst) = low32(src) & sext(mask); if low32(src) != 0 jump
  xband32_s8_br_if_not_x32   low32(dst) = low32(src) & sext(mask); if low32(src) == 0 jump
  xband64_s8_br_if_x64       dst        = src        & sext(mask); if src        != 0 jump
  xband64_s8_br_if_not_x64   dst        = src        & sext(mask); if src        == 0 jump

The forward/inverted pairs let the Cranelift Pulley backend's MachBuffer
flip branch direction for fallthrough optimization without losing the
fusion. The 32-bit and 64-bit variants cover the pointer-width split
across aarch64-apple-darwin/-ios (64-bit) and arm64_32-apple-watchos
(32-bit) target deployments.

These ops are emitted by the Cranelift Pulley backend at the call_indirect
lazy-init brif site, fusing the masked-funcref AND with the null-check
branch into a single match_loop dispatch — the smallest viable step on
the "next branch -- opcode fusion" track from PR #2's description.
